From 05106e0bb7e30caad2572140565e670468053099 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:20:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: free a link station of a removed link without a
 disconnection

hostapd_free_link_stas() frees, on a link that leaves the AP MLD, the
link stations of the non-AP MLDs associated over another link. Each
went through ap_free_sta() and its ap_sta_set_authorized(..., 0), which
reported AP-STA-DISCONNECTED and a ubus "disassoc" event with the MLD
address. A non-AP MLD that stays associated over its other links was
then reported gone.

Clear the authorized flag of such a link station without the event
before it is freed.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 src/ap/sta_info.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -606,6 +606,7 @@ void hostapd_free_link_stas(struct hosta
 
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Removing link station from MLD " MACSTR,
 			   MAC2STR(prev->addr));
+		ap_sta_set_authorized_flag(hapd, prev, 0);
 		ap_free_sta(hapd, prev);
 	}
 }
